# Platform documentation sync

When you add, remove, or change **user-visible behavior** in this repo, update the platform docs in the **same change set** (same commit when committing):

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| New/removed/renamed command or alias | `docs/PLATFORM_COMMANDS.md` |
| Command behavior, permission, or grouping | `docs/PLATFORM_COMMANDS.md` |
| New/removed/changed feature, GUI flow, policy, integration | `docs/PLATFORM_FEATURES.md` |
| Both command and feature | Both files + `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` |
| GUIs, architecture, config file map (detail) | `docs/PLATFORM_REFERENCE.md` when the overview is affected |

**Do not** only update `PLATFORM_REFERENCE.md` when commands or the feature list changed — the copy-paste files are the source of truth for those two lists.

**Files:**

- `docs/PLATFORM_FEATURES.md` — flat, copy-paste feature list by plugin
- `docs/PLATFORM_COMMANDS.md` — flat, copy-paste command trees and permissions
- `docs/PLATFORM_REFERENCE.md` — GUIs, integration diagrams, config tables

After tag releases, optionally bump the "Bundle baseline" line at the top of FEATURES and COMMANDS when the user asks to up tags.
